      "answer": "Southwest's 737 MAX 8 fleet (87 aircraft as of January 1, 2024) is compliant with FAA AD 2020-05-11 (pre-service compliance November 2020) and FAA AD 2022-03-07 (completed April 2022). For FAA AD 2024-01-02 (MCAS Software v2.0 installation), compliance is due by May 15, 2024: all 87 aircraft currently run MCAS v1.7.3, with software updates scheduled February-May 2024 (phased, ~10 aircraft/month) to reach MCAS v2.0 (Boeing SB, Rev2). The fleet was grounded March 13, 2019 per FAA Emergency Order and returned to revenue service March 11, 2021.",
